GOAL: a fully agentic ChangeGuard, triggered ONLY by `git commit`.
Picture: a "doctor" agent (changeguard_supervisor, in watsonx Orchestrate) decides every step; a "nurse"
(the local AGENT RUNTIME in services/backend) phones the doctor, tells her which tools exist, runs only the
tools she asks for (if allowed) and reports results back. All calls go OUTBOUND from the laptop to Orchestrate.
No tunnel, no inbound access, no prepared tests or fixes, no project-specific hints in agent instructions.
Windows + Git Bash. Never print or log secrets. Do not change approval binding, executor checks or verdict
computation. All existing tests must keep passing.
Read .bob/rules/changeguard.md, plans/CONTRACTS.md, agents/, scripts/hooks/, scripts/install-hook.sh,
services/backend (wxo.ts, runs.ts, direct.ts, summary) and services/changeguard-tools first.
Plan all phases now; implement ONE phase at a time and stop for my review after each.

PHASE 1 — Trigger: git commit only
- scripts/hooks/post-commit: on any branch except main, send {source:"git-hook", repo_path, branch, head_sha} to
  POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/runs and return immediately (background; never slow down, block or fail the commit;
  if the backend is down, print one line and exit 0). Keep the Windows notification and browser-open.
- scripts/install-hook.sh <repo path> / scripts/uninstall-hook.sh: install via core.hooksPath for that repo,
  keeping any existing hooks working. Install it for fixture/target-enterprise-app.
- Backend inputs, live: base = merge-base(main, head_sha), head = head_sha; ticket = first [A-Z]+-[0-9]+ in the branch
  name or commit subject; requirement = tickets/<ID>.md if present, else the commit body, else status needs_input.
  demo-work is synced to head_sha through the existing safe reset path (marker/origin checks unchanged).
- One run per commit SHA (same SHA → return the existing run). A newer commit on the same branch marks older running
  runs of that branch "superseded".
- Remove other automatic starts: Bob's Reviewer mode no longer starts runs by itself (it only reports, see Phase 4);
  the manual start form stays hidden under "Advanced" for testing only.

PHASE 2 — The agent runtime ("nurse"), services/backend/src/agentic/
- Protocol (document in CONTRACTS.md as v2.0 "agentic runtime"):
  run_start → {"type":"run_start", run_id, change:{ticket, requirement, branch, base, head}, tools:[{name, description,
  args_schema}], agents:[{name, purpose, input_schema}], limits:{max_steps, steps_used}}
  supervisor reply (JSON only, exactly one action):
   {"thought":"<≤2 sentences>","action":"call_tool","tool":"<name>","args":{...}}
   {"thought":"...","action":"consult_agent","agent":"<name>","input":{...}}
   {"thought":"...","action":"finish","report":{"summary","risks":[...],"recommendation"}}
  observation → {"type":"observation", step, ok, result (trimmed to 12 KB, say if trimmed), error?,
  state:{proof_status?, proposal_id?, findings_count, steps_used}}
  post_approval → {"type":"post_approval", reverify, verdict}; the supervisor only writes the final narrative.
- Tool registry (registry.ts, the single source of truth sent in run_start): get_git_diff, analyze_blast_radius,
  run_security_rules, write_and_run_tests, submit_patch_proposal (existing tools, called locally), plus NEW read-only
  read_file(path, start_line, end_line; ≤200 lines) and search_code(pattern; ≤50 results), limited to WORK_ROOT src/
  and tests/, rejecting path escapes. Each tool has a JSON schema. There is NO apply tool.
- Loop: send → strict JSON parse (strip code fences; invalid → one error message and one retry) → validate against the
  registry and schema (unknown tool, bad args, path escape → error observation) → execute → observe → repeat until
  finish or a limit. Conversation memory: use the Orchestrate thread id if wxo.ts supports it, else resend a compact
  history of previous actions and results.
- Limits: MAX_AGENT_STEPS=25, 2 retries per tool, 90 s per agent call, 10 min per run → NEEDS_REVIEW with the reason.
- Every thought, action and observation is stored as an evidence event (no secrets, trimmed).
- ORCHESTRATOR_MODE=agentic is the default; direct stays for unit tests only and is labelled "test mode".
- After the supervisor finishes with a stored proposal → run waits for human approval in Mission Control (unchanged);
  after apply + re-verify, send post_approval and store the supervisor's final narrative. Verdict = backend rules.

PHASE 3 — The agents ("doctor" + specialists), agents/*.yaml, no tools, JSON only, generic instructions
- changeguard_supervisor: "You cannot run anything. The first message lists the tools and agents you may use; use
  only those names, one action per reply, and wait for each result. Never claim a result you have not received."
  Typical good plan: diff → blast radius → rules → impact_analyst → test_writer → write_and_run_tests (new test if
  INCONCLUSIVE) → fix_writer → submit_patch_proposal (retry if check fails) → reviewer → finish. Explain skips in thought.
- changeguard_impact_analyst (risky consumers, why, path to test), changeguard_test_writer (one Jest TS test through
  the producer entry point found in the evidence; retry input has proof_status/invalid_reason/messages),
  changeguard_fix_writer (minimal unified diff, src/ only, ≤40 lines, no test edits; retry input has the git error),
  changeguard_reviewer (acceptance criteria covered/missing, labelled "opinion").
  Exact input/output JSON in each file. consult_agent calls the named agent through wxo.ts.
- Validate with the wxo-builder skill and watsonx-orchestrate-adk-docs; deploy with the orchestrate CLI; put the ids in
  services/backend/.env as WXO_AGENT_ID_SUPERVISOR, _IMPACT, _TEST, _FIX, _REVIEW (never print other values).
- Smoke test: send the supervisor a run_start with two tools via `orchestrate chat ask`; it must reply with one valid
  call_tool action naming a listed tool.

PHASE 4 — Where the developer sees it
- Mission Control: an "Agent timeline" (step, agent, thought, action, short result, duration) on the run page; which
  agent wrote the test and the fix; steps and retries; the commit (branch, short SHA, message) that triggered it.
- Windows notification when the run reaches awaiting_approval or finishes: headline + link.
- Bob Reviewer mode (update .bob/reviewer-instructions.md): does NOT start runs; at the start of every reply calls
  get_latest_run for the current branch and, if there is a new result, reports it first with the agreed template
  (headline, where + "not in your diff", Proof (tested), Fix ready + link, Bob's review (opinion)).

PHASE 5 — Tests and live verification (save to docs/evidence/agentic-commit/)
- Unit tests (chat API mocked): happy path; invalid JSON then valid; unknown tool; bad args; read_file path escape;
  INCONCLUSIVE then a new test; rejected diff then fixed; step limit → NEEDS_REVIEW; timeout; agent asks to apply →
  refused; same SHA → same run; newer SHA → older run superseded; hook never fails the commit when the backend is down.
- Live: with scripts/start-demo.sh running, in fixture/target-enterprise-app make a small commit on
  feature/promo-null-discount (e.g. a comment) → the run starts by itself, the agents work, Mission Control shows the
  timeline, approve, verdict "PASSED — within tested scope". Repeat 3 times (reset between runs).
  Then create branch feature/price-150 with a NEW change the agents have never seen (make Product.cost nullable and add
  tickets/PRICE-150.md) and commit → report honestly what the agents did.
  Per run: steps, agents consulted, retries, first test VALID?, first diff applied?, durations, verdict.
- Update README (install the hook, how it works) and plans/SUBMISSION.md ("triggered by git commit; fully agentic on
  watsonx Orchestrate; outbound only; a human approves every fix; the verdict is computed by rules, not by the AI").
